  "claim": "The character Sylvia Hollamby was played by one actor for all eight series. This actor starred in a Polanski film in 1965.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Helen Fraser (actress). Sentence: Helen Fraser (born Helen Margaret Stronach; born 15 June 1942 in Oldham, Lancashire) is an English actress, who has appeared in many television series since the early 1960s.\nPage: Helen Fraser (actress). Sentence: For international audiences, she may be best known for her roles in \"Billy Liar\" (1963) and \"Repulsion\" (1965).\nPage: Repulsion (film). Sentence: Repulsion is a 1965 British psychological horror film directed by Roman Polanski, and starring Catherine Deneuve, Ian Hendry, John Fraser and Yvonne Furneaux.\nPage: Sylvia Hollamby. Sentence: Portrayed by Helen Fraser from the first episode in 1999 until the last in 2006, she was the longest serving prison officer on the show with convicts Julie Johnston (Kika Mirylees) and Julie Saunders (Victoria Alcock) being the only other characters to last all eight series.",
