        "original_id": "d16e2a03-1996-5e5a-9cd4-17d809f0b7ad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Helen Fraser, Roman Polanski, Catherine Deneuve, Ian Hendry, John Fraser, Yvonne Furneaux, Kika Mirylees, Victoria Alcock\n- Roles: Sylvia Hollamby, Julie Johnston, Julie Saunders\n- Works: Billy Liar, Repulsion, Bad Girls\n- Places: Oldham, Lancashire\n\nFacts:\n- Helen Fraser, born Helen Margaret Stronach on 15 June 1942 in Oldham, Lancashire, is an English actress.\n- Helen Fraser has appeared in many television series since the early 1960s.\n- Helen Fraser is known internationally for roles in the films Billy Liar (1963) and Repulsion (1965).\n- Repulsion is a 1965 British psychological horror film directed by Roman Polanski and starring Catherine Deneuve, Ian Hendry, John Fraser, and Yvonne Furneaux.\n- Helen Fraser portrayed Sylvia Hollamby from the first episode in 1999 to the final episode in 2006.\n- Sylvia Hollamby was the longest-serving prison officer on the show, and Julie Johnston, played by Kika Mirylees, and Julie Saunders, played by Victoria Alcock, were the only other characters to appear in all eight series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
